# 10. Compliance and Security Requirements

## Regulatory Requirements

| Regulation | Requirement | Impact |
|---|---|---|
| HIPAA | Protect PHI at rest and in transit | Encryption, access controls, audit logging |
| SOC 2 | Trust Services Criteria for security | Access controls, monitoring, incident response |
| ISO 27001 | Information security management | Policy, risk assessment, controls |
| ISO 9001 | Quality management | Document control, version control |
| QMS | Quality management system | SOPs, training records, CAPA |

## Security Controls

| Control | Requirement |
|---|---|
| Authentication | Multi-factor authentication for all users |
| Authorization | Role-based access control (RBAC) |
| Encryption | AES-256 at rest, TLS 1.2+ in transit |
| Audit Logging | All access and changes logged |
| Data Retention | PHI retained per HIPAA requirements |
| Incident Response | Documented and tested |
| Access Review | Quarterly reviews of user access |

## Audit Readiness

- All requirements traceable to source
- Document control with version history
- Objective evidence collected and stored
- CAPA tracking for findings
- Management review inputs prepared
